/**
 * The `border-inline-end-style` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
 * defines the style of the logical inline end border of an element, which maps to a physical border
 * style depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation. It
 * corresponds to the `border-top-style`, `border-right-style`, `border-bottom-style`, or
 * `border-left-style` property depending on the values defined for `writing-mode`, `direction`, and
 * `text-orientation`.
 *
 * Initial: none. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Grammar: <line-style>
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#propdef-border-inline-end-style
 *
 * Author guide:
